{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310720,"nonce":"/UpNus2Irv6lw2FQeLv3SOzi50M=","title":"String.substr(pos) 1-arg form silently SIGILL'd because only the 2-arg mapping was registered — FIXED in 65b5cf6","message":"`s.substr(pos)` (one-arg form, \"from pos to end\") silently SIGILL'd. Only `params: 2` was registered in `runtime_mapping.rs`; the 1-arg call fell through to name-only resolution and was lowered as an indirect call against the wrong signature.\n\nFixed in `65b5cf6` (`fix(stdlib): add 1-arg String.substr wrapper + param-count dispatch`):\n\n1. `String_substr_1` MIR wrapper at [string.rs:386+](compiler/src/stdlib/string.rs) — calls `haxe_string_length`, computes `len - pos`, forwards to `haxe_string_substr_ptr`.\n2. `params: 1` runtime mapping entry pointing at the wrapper.\n3. Added `\"substr\"` to the param-count-aware dispatch allowlist at [hir_to_mir.rs:9218](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L9218) (joined `\"indexOf\"` and `\"lastIndexOf\"`).\n\n**Why this lay dormant:** Most stdlib code paths happen to call the 2-arg form. The 1-arg call appears in user code that's UTF-8-string-heavy (BPE tokenization, splitter helpers), which is rare outside ML use cases. Llama-smoke's `parseMerge` was the first hit.\n\n**How to apply (generalization):**\n- For any other overloaded stdlib method with multiple arities, both the MIR wrappers AND the dispatch allowlist need to include the method name. Search for `mn == \"indexOf\"` in `hir_to_mir.rs` — that's the central allowlist.\n- Pattern for \"default the trailing optional arg\": MIR wrapper calls another runtime helper (often `_length`) to compute the default and forwards.\n- Mirror existing `String_indexOf` / `String_lastIndexOf` 1-arg wrappers — they follow the same shape.\n\n**Related/follow-up.** Llama-smoke now runs end-to-end (load 4.92 GB GGUF, build 128256-token vocab, parse 280147 merges, print vocab sample, exit 0). Remaining cosmetic: `bos id: 0` / `eos id: 0` instead of expected 128000/128001 — likely a switch-case binding issue in `registerSpecial`'s pattern over the `U8|I8|U16|I16|U32|I32|U64|I64` enum variants (not all variants are binding the captured `id` correctly). Separate from substr.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_substr_1arg` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}